 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Multitexturing DVR
-A hardware-accelerated DVR algorithm based on register combiners and multitexturing [S3]. It sets itself apart from siblings by using a viewing-direction-based dynamic texture slice resampling scheme that maintains a constant step size to avoid striping artifacts [S3]. Choose it when interactive performance on commodity hardware is required and viewing direction changes frequently [S3]. See [Multi-Texture Interpolation](2200-multi-texture-interpolation.md).
